---
source: crates/ibis-cli/tests/human_output.rs
expression: said
---
$ ibis --file errors.bib cite first absent
exit 4
stderr| ibis: no reference has the citation key 'absent'; find the right key with: ibis search <words>

$ ibis --file errors.bib show absent
exit 4
stderr| ibis: no reference has the citation key 'absent'; find the right key with: ibis search <words>

$ ibis --file duplicate-one.bib --file duplicate-two.bib cite same
exit 3
stderr| ibis: several references use the citation key 'same'; give each one its own key in your library.

$ ibis --file /invented/missing.bib search x
exit 5
stderr| ibis: cannot open /invented/missing.bib: there is no file at that path; check the spelling or give the full path.

$ ibis --file <tmp> search x
exit 3
stderr| ibis: cannot open <tmp>: it is a folder; give the library file inside it.

$ ibis show anything (no library)
exit 4
stderr| ibis: cannot look up 'anything': no library is open; add --file <library> or --zotero.

$ ibis search anything (no library)
exit 0
stdout| No library is open; add --file <library> or --zotero.

$ ibis search x --limit 5000
exit 2
stderr| ibis: invalid value '5000' for '--limit <N>': give a whole number from 1 to 1000
stderr| 
stderr|   For more information, try '--help'.

$ ibis call invented
exit 2
stderr| ibis: there is no method 'invented'; choose one of: libraries, search, show, cite, project, entry, styles, outputs, schema, call

$ ibis call search --params {
exit 3
stderr| ibis: --params must be the JSON parameters of search; see: ibis schema search

$ ibis search
exit 2
stderr| ibis: the following required arguments were not provided:
stderr|     <WORDS>
stderr| 
stderr|   Usage: ibis search <WORDS>
stderr| 
stderr|   For more information, try '--help'.

$ ibis show --id nonsense
exit 3
stderr| ibis: --id must be a reference's id, the JSON that ibis search --json prints.

$ ibis show absent --json
exit 4
stdout| {"error":{"code":"not-found"},"ibis":1,"ok":false}
stderr| ibis: no reference has the citation key 'absent'; find the right key with: ibis search <words>
